# Files both sides write to, where a merge should keep what each added rather than stop on a
# conflict: the changelog the project and this fork each append to, and the settings the fork's
# own rows sit in the middle of.
#
# The nightly merge is what this is for (see .github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml): a union cannot
# drop a line, so the worst a merge of these two can do is fail to compile - and a release is
# only published after a build that passed, so that cannot reach a player. A conflict anywhere
# else still stops the job, which leaves the newest release exactly where it was.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
crates/omsi-app/src/settings.rs merge=union
